 "_comment": "Driving situations used as stimuli. clip: source dashcam video (not in git). start_s/duration_s: the part of it used. event_s: when the car reacts, in source-clip seconds; the display is shown around it. why/how/manoeuvre: the explanation texts. geometry: overlay geometry for the clip, from the perception pipeline (data/geometry_pipeline/, which also holds the camera calibration it found); empty = data/geometry/<id>_geometry.jsonl.gz, written by extract_geometry.py. camera: flat-ground constants at 1280x720, given only where the pipeline's auto-calibration found none; they then win over the geometry's (check them with render_stimuli.py --calibrate). comprehension: the clip stops at stop_s (source-clip seconds) and the participant answers what the car does next; correct must match what the footage shows after stop_s. verified: whether a person checked the answer against the footage. country: ISO 3166 code of where the clip was filmed (compared with participants' country of residence). criticality: low or high, how risky the situation is; the analysis compares preferences between the two. source: the dataset video and its start in it. event_checked: whether a person checked event_s against the footage (propose_events.py proposes it). texts_verified: whether a person checked the why/how/manoeuvre texts against the footage (the how part is a guess from still frames until then).",
